# Point data and interpretation

- Keep `PointsData` as a raw decoder of the per-point `points_data` bytes.
  Rename `raw*` accessors to `get*`, returning stored values without
  normalization, constant fallback, or derived calculations. Move interpreted
  and derived accessors (including `height` and `secondaryScale`) out of it.
- Add a `drawing.StrokeData` wrapper that retains `proto.StrokeData`, owns
  the decoded `points_constant_flags` / `points_constant_values`, and holds
  the raw `PointsData`. Keep point-level interpreted and derived accessors
  off this wrapper.
- Provide a separate resolved point view that combines per-point channels
  with stroke-wide constants and supplies normalized and derived values.
  Establish the constant-table wire layout, precedence when both masks set
  a channel, and defaults when neither does before implementing resolution.
- Test varying-only and constant-only channels, derived values combining
  both sources, overlapping masks, absent channels, and malformed constant
  data. Resolve the existing width/height discrepancy against the notes.

Update the sources in `src/skel/java/` and regenerate `src/main/java/` when
changing generated drawing classes.
